---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Simon"
  description="Simon is a private, personal chief-of-staff productivity system built and operated by Logan Lyle for his own use."
>
  <div class="eyebrow">Simon / Chief of Staff</div>
  <h1>Simon — Personal Chief of Staff</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Simon is a private, personal productivity system I built and use for my own
    chief-of-staff work — email, calendar, files, and task tracking across accounts I
    personally own and operate.
  </p>

  <p><strong>This is not a public product.</strong> It isn't available to anyone else, and
    it doesn't manage data on behalf of anyone other than me.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>What Simon does</h2>
    <p>Across a small set of Google accounts I personally own, Simon is authorized to:</p>
    <ul class="check">
      <li><strong>Gmail</strong> — read, search, and organize mail (labels, archiving,
        trash/restore); draft messages; send email only where I've explicitly
        pre-authorized it.</li>
      <li><strong>Calendar</strong> — read events across connected calendars; create,
        edit, reschedule, or cancel events where explicitly authorized.</li>
      <li><strong>Drive</strong> — search and read existing files; create new files;
        organize, move, and update files where explicitly authorized.</li>
      <li><strong>Docs &amp; Sheets</strong> — read, create, and edit documents and
        spreadsheets where explicitly authorized.</li>
      <li><strong>Contacts</strong> — read, create, and update personal contacts where
        explicitly authorized.</li>
      <li><strong>Tasks</strong> — read and manage task lists and tasks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Runs on infrastructure I control, using Anthropic's Claude models to process and
      reason over that information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Separately, for my own primary Google account only, I also use Google's own
      first-party connector for Claude to read Calendar and Drive — that connection is
      authorized, governed, and operated directly by
      <a href="https://www.anthropic.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anthropic</a>,
      not by this application, and isn't covered by the scopes described here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Simon doesn't do</h2>
    <ul class="check">
      <li>Doesn't sell data, in any form, to anyone.</li>
      <li>Doesn't use data for advertising or build advertising profiles.</li>
      <li>Doesn't share data with third parties, other than the infrastructure and API
        providers required to run it.</li>
      <li>Doesn't act on, or gain access to, any account I haven't explicitly
        connected.</li>
      <li>Doesn't permanently delete mail, files, contacts, or calendar events unless
        I've explicitly authorized that specific action — routine deletions go through
        normal reversible mechanisms (e.g. Gmail Trash) wherever the underlying Google
        product offers one.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Access &amp; revocation</h2>
    <p>
      Because Simon connects through standard Google OAuth, I can review or revoke its
      access at any time from my Google Account's
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Security → Third-party access
      </a> settings, the same as any other connected app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:loganlyle55@gmail.com">loganlyle55@gmail.com</a></p>
    <p><a href="/privacy/">Read the full Privacy Policy →</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
